# SIMPLE WAY TO THINK ABOUT EVERYTHING

## The Full Git/GitHub Process

- I write code.

- Git tracks my changes.

- I stage the changes:

    git add .

- I save them as a commit:

    git commit -m "Add feature"

- I upload the commit to GitHub:

    git push

- Someone else can download my changes:

    git pull

- If I want to work on something separately:

    git switch -c feature-name

- When I finish:

    Push branch
        ↓
    Pull Request
        ↓
    Code review
        ↓
    Merge
        ↓
    Main branch

- This is the basic system behind how many software development teams work.

